<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S8.Ex13.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{c}p_{v}(c)\,H(p_{v}(\cdot|c))+\sum_{c}p_{v}(c)\,d_{\textsf{KL}}(p_{v}(\cdot|c)\,\|\,\hat{p}_{M}(\cdot|c))," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>c</mi></munder></mstyle><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>c</mi></munder></mstyle><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">KL</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0.337em">∥</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>M</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{c}p_{v}(c)\,H(p_{v}(\cdot|c))+\sum_{c}p_{v}(c)\,d_{\textsf{KL}}(p_{v}(\cdot|c)\,\|\,\hat{p}_{M}(\cdot|c)),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S8.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S8.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(a)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(a)</annotation></semantics></math> follows by regrouping terms in the summation to be over all word-context tuples in the test sequence, <math id="S8.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(b)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(b)</annotation></semantics></math> follows from <math id="S8.SS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{cw}=p_{v}(c)p_{v}(w|c)\,T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{cw}=p_{v}(c)p_{v}(w|c)\,T</annotation></semantics></math> by definition.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S8.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S8.SS2.4" class="ltx_text">VIII-B</span> </span><span id="S8.SS2.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Proof of Theorem <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem III.1 ‣ III-C KL proximity ‣ III Embeddings, Semantic Similarity and Proximity in KL Distance ‣ Semantic Smoothing for Language Models via Distribution Estimation and Embeddings" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">III.1</span></a></span></h3>

<div id="S8.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let</p>
<table id="S8.EGx7" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S8.Ex14"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S8.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle Z</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S8.Ex14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{y\in V}\exp(g_{y}(f_{c})+\epsilon_{c,y}))," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">OPEN</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{y\in V}\exp(g_{y}(f_{c})+\epsilon_{c,y})),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S8.Ex15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S8.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\tilde{Z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\tilde{Z}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S8.Ex15.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{y\in V}\exp(g_{y}(f_{\tilde{c}})+\epsilon_{\tilde{c},y}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">OPEN</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{y\in V}\exp(g_{y}(f_{\tilde{c}})+\epsilon_{\tilde{c},y}))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S8.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">denote the denominators of the next-word probability expression in (<a href="#S3.E5" title="In Definition 1 ((𝐿,ϵ)-Lipschitz-logit process) ‣ III-B Embeddings to next-word probabilities: Lipschitzness ‣ III Embeddings, Semantic Similarity and Proximity in KL Distance ‣ Semantic Smoothing for Language Models via Distribution Estimation and Embeddings" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>). Now,</p>
<table id="S8.EGx8" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_eqnarray ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S8.E22"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S8.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\log\frac{\tilde{Z}}{Z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>Z</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\log\frac{\tilde{Z}}{Z}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S8.Ex16.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
