<section id="S8.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S8.SS3.4" class="ltx_text">VIII-C</span> </span><span id="S8.SS3.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Proof of Corollary <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem2" title="Corollary III.2 ‣ III-C KL proximity ‣ III Embeddings, Semantic Similarity and Proximity in KL Distance ‣ Semantic Smoothing for Language Models via Distribution Estimation and Embeddings" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">III.2</span></a></span></h3>

<div id="S8.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The proof follows directly from Theorem <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem III.1 ‣ III-C KL proximity ‣ III Embeddings, Semantic Similarity and Proximity in KL Distance ‣ Semantic Smoothing for Language Models via Distribution Estimation and Embeddings" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">III.1</span></a> and the <math id="S8.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{f}</annotation></semantics></math>-Lipschitzness.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S8.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S8.SS4.4" class="ltx_text">VIII-D</span> </span><span id="S8.SS4.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Proof of Theorem <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem IV.2 ‣ IV-A Minimax distribution estimation with side information ‣ IV Distribution Estimation under KL Loss with KL Proximity Side Information ‣ Semantic Smoothing for Language Models via Distribution Estimation and Embeddings" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">IV.2</span></a></span></h3>

<div id="S8.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Note from <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">26</a>, Theorem 2.7.2]</cite> that the KL–divergence is convex in the second argument. From this, we have</p>
<table id="S8.EGx11" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_eqnarray ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S8.E25"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td colspan="3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell">max_<span id="S8.E25.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">π</span>∈B_<span id="S8.E25.1.1.2" class="ltx_text">KL</span>(<span id="S8.E25.1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">π</span>^(0), Δ) <span id="S8.E25.1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_blackboard">E</span>[d_<span id="S8.E25.1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_sansserif">KL</span>(<span id="S8.E25.1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">π</span>∥ 
                      ^
                      
                        <span id="S8.E25.1.1.7.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">π</span>
                      
                    )]</td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="3" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(25)</span></td></tr>
<tr class="ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S8.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S8.Ex23.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\max_{\pi\in B_{\text{KL}}(\pi^{(0)},\Delta)}\left(\alpha\mathbb{E}[d_{\textsf{KL}}(\pi\|\hat{\pi}_{\textsf{opt}})]+(1-\alpha)d_{\textsf{KL}}(\pi\|\pi^{(0)})\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mtext>KL</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>α</mi><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">KL</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">opt</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">KL</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\max_{\pi\in B_{\text{KL}}(\pi^{(0)},\Delta)}\left(\alpha\mathbb{E}[d_{\textsf{KL}}(\pi\|\hat{\pi}_{\textsf{opt}})]+(1-\alpha)d_{\textsf{KL}}(\pi\|\pi^{(0)})\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr class="ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S8.E25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S8.E25.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\alpha\left(\frac{d-1}{2n}+o\left(\frac{1}{n}\right)\right)+(1-\alpha)\Delta." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\alpha\left(\frac{d-1}{2n}+o\left(\frac{1}{n}\right)\right)+(1-\alpha)\Delta.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S8.SS4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Picking <math id="S8.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> to be <math id="S8.SS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="S8.SS4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math> depending on the relative values of the two terms gives the desired result.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S8.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S8.SS5.4" class="ltx_text">VIII-E</span> </span><span id="S8.SS5.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Proof of Theorem <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem IV.3 ‣ IV-A Minimax distribution estimation with side information ‣ IV Distribution Estimation under KL Loss with KL Proximity Side Information ‣ Semantic Smoothing for Language Models via Distribution Estimation and Embeddings" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">IV.3</span></a></span></h3>

<div id="S8.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">First, note that</p>
<table id="S8.EGx12" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_eqnarray ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S8.E26"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td colspan="3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell">min_
                      ^
                      
                        <span id="S8.E26.1.1.1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">π</span>
                      
                     max_<span id="S8.E26.1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">π</span>∈B_<span id="S8.E26.1.1.3" class="ltx_text">KL</span>(<span id="S8.E26.1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">π</span>^(0), Δ) <span id="S8.E26.1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_blackboard">E</span>[d_<span id="S8.E26.1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_sansserif">KL</span>(<span id="S8.E26.1.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">π</span>∥ 
                      ^
                      
                        <span id="S8.E26.1.1.8.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">π</span>
                      
                    )]</td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="3" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(26)</span></td></tr>
<tr class="ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S8.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\overset{(a)}{\geq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">a</mi><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">)</mo></mrow></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\overset{(a)}{\geq}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S8.Ex25.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\min_{\hat{\pi}}\max_{\pi\in B_{\text{KL}}(\pi^{(0)},\Delta)}\frac{\mathbb{E}[\|\pi-\hat{\pi}\|_{1}^{2}]}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mtext>KL</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\min_{\hat{\pi}}\max_{\pi\in B_{\text{KL}}(\pi^{(0)},\Delta)}\frac{\mathbb{E}[\|\pi-\hat{\pi}\|_{1}^{2}]}{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr class="ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S8.E26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\overset{(b)}{\geq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">b</mi><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">)</mo></mrow></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\overset{(b)}{\geq}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S8.E26.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\min_{\hat{\pi}}\max_{\pi\in B_{\text{KL}}(\pi^{(0)},\Delta)}\frac{\mathbb{E}[\|\pi-\hat{\pi}\|_{1}]^{2}}{2}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mtext>KL</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\min_{\hat{\pi}}\max_{\pi\in B_{\text{KL}}(\pi^{(0)},\Delta)}\frac{\mathbb{E}[\|\pi-\hat{\pi}\|_{1}]^{2}}{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S8.SS5.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S8.SS5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(a)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(a)</annotation></semantics></math> follows from Pinsker’s inequality and <math id="S8.SS5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(b)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(b)</annotation></semantics></math> follows using <math id="S8.SS5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[X^{2}]\geq\mathbb{E}[X]^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[X^{2}]\geq\mathbb{E}[X]^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. In the rest of the proof, we lower bound the <math id="S8.SS5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> norm error using Assouad’s lemma <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib10" title="" class="ltx_ref">27</a>]</cite> and use (<a href="#S8.E26" title="In VIII-E Proof of Theorem ‣ VIII Proofs of Theorems ‣ Semantic Smoothing for Language Models via Distribution Estimation and Embeddings" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">26</span></a>) to get a lower bound on the KL–divergence.</p>
</div>
<div id="S8.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S8.Thmtheorem1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma VIII.1</span></span><span id="S8.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> (Assouad’s Lemma)</span></h6>
<div id="S8.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S8.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Consider distributions <math id="S8.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{v}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{v}</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="S8.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> letters, where <math id="S8.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\in\{-1,1\}^{l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mi>l</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\in\{-1,1\}^{l}</annotation></semantics></math>, such that</span></p>
<table id="S8.E27" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S8.E27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\min_{a\in\mathcal{A}}\left(L(\theta_{v},a)+L(\theta_{v^{\prime}},a)\right)\geq\lambda\cdot d_{H}(v,v^{\prime})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>H</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\min_{a\in\mathcal{A}}\left(L(\theta_{v},a)+L(\theta_{v^{\prime}},a)\right)\geq\lambda\cdot d_{H}(v,v^{\prime}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(27)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S8.Thmtheorem1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S8.Thmtheorem1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="S8.Thmtheorem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math> is a family of distributions on <math id="S8.Thmtheorem1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> letters, <math id="S8.Thmtheorem1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L(\cdot,\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L(\cdot,\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> is a real-valued loss function defined between distributions, <math id="S8.Thmtheorem1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{H}(\cdot,\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{H}(\cdot,\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> denotes Hamming distance between vectors and <math id="S8.Thmtheorem1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math> is a constant. Then,</span></p>
<table id="S8.E28" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S8.E28.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\min_{\hat{\theta}}\max_{\theta\in\mathcal{A}}L(\theta,\hat{\theta})\geq\frac{l\lambda}{4}\exp(-n\max\limits_{v,v^{\prime}:d_{H}(v,v^{\prime})=1}d_{\textsf{KL}}(\theta_{v}\|\theta_{v^{\prime}}))." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></munder><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow></munder><mi>L</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>θ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>n</mi><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif-italic">KL</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\min_{\hat{\theta}}\max_{\theta\in\mathcal{A}}L(\theta,\hat{\theta})\geq\frac{l\lambda}{4}\exp(-n\max\limits_{v,v^{\prime}:d_{H}(v,v^{\prime})=1}d_{\textsf{KL}}(\theta_{v}\|\theta_{v^{\prime}})).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(28)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S8.SS5.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.SS5.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Without loss of generality, assume that <math id="S8.SS5.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> is even. We take <math id="S8.SS5.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l=\frac{d}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l=\frac{d}{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S8.SS5.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}=B_{\text{KL}}(\pi^{(0)},\Delta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mtext>KL</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}=B_{\text{KL}}(\pi^{(0)},\Delta)</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="S8.SS5.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{(0)}=\Unif[d]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝖴𝗇𝗂𝖿</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{(0)}=\Unif[d]</annotation></semantics></math>, and the loss <math id="S8.SS5.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> to be the expected <math id="S8.SS5.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>–norm. Clearly, <math id="S8.SS5.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\in\{-1,+1\}^{\frac{d}{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\in\{-1,+1\}^{\frac{d}{2}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Define <math id="S8.SS5.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{v}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{v}</annotation></semantics></math> as follows:</p>
<table id="S8.E29" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S8.E29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{v}=\left(\frac{1}{d}+\tau v_{1},\frac{1}{d}-\tau v_{1},\dots,\frac{1}{d}+\tau v_{\frac{d}{2}},\frac{1}{d}-\tau v_{\frac{d}{2}}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>d</mi></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>d</mi></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>d</mi></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>d</mi></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{v}=\left(\frac{1}{d}+\tau v_{1},\frac{1}{d}-\tau v_{1},\dots,\frac{1}{d}+\tau v_{\frac{d}{2}},\frac{1}{d}-\tau v_{\frac{d}{2}}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(29)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S8.SS5.p3" class="ltx_para">
<ol id="S8.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S8.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="S8.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To ensure non-negativity of coordinates, we need <math id="S8.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau\leq\frac{1}{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>d</mi></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau\leq\frac{1}{d}</annotation></semantics></math>. We take <math id="S8.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau\leq\frac{1}{2d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau\leq\frac{1}{2d}</annotation></semantics></math> to ensure each <math id="S8.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{d}-\tau\geq\frac{1}{2d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>d</mi></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{d}-\tau\geq\frac{1}{2d}</annotation></semantics></math>. It can be seen that <math id="S8.I1.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{v}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{v}</annotation></semantics></math> is a valid distribution for <math id="S8.I1.i1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\geq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\geq 2</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S8.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="S8.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To ensure that <math id="S8.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{v}\in B_{\text{KL}}(\pi^{(0)},\Delta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mtext>KL</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{v}\in B_{\text{KL}}(\pi^{(0)},\Delta)</annotation></semantics></math>, note that we need <math id="S8.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="d_{\textsf{KL}}(\theta_{v}\|\pi^{(0)})\leq\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">KL</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\textsf{KL}}(\theta_{v}\|\pi^{(0)})\leq\Delta</annotation></semantics></math>. The sum of the <math id="S8.I1.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(2i-1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(2i-1)</annotation></semantics></math>-th term and the <math id="S8.I1.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(2i)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(2i)</annotation></semantics></math>-th term in the KL–divergence is</p>
<table id="S8.E30" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S8.E30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left(\frac{1}{d}+\tau v_{i}\right)\log\left(\frac{\frac{1}{d}+\tau v_{i}}{\frac{1}{d}}\right)\\
+\left(\frac{1}{d}-\tau v_{i}\right)\log\left(\frac{\frac{1}{d}-\tau v_{i}}{\frac{1}{d}}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>d</mi></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>d</mi></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>d</mi></mfrac></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>d</mi></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>d</mi></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>d</mi></mfrac></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left(\frac{1}{d}+\tau v_{i}\right)\log\left(\frac{\frac{1}{d}+\tau v_{i}}{\frac{1}{d}}\right)\\
+\left(\frac{1}{d}-\tau v_{i}\right)\log\left(\frac{\frac{1}{d}-\tau v_{i}}{\frac{1}{d}}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(30)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S8.I1.i2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Since <math id="S8.I1.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau\leq\frac{1}{2d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau\leq\frac{1}{2d}</annotation></semantics></math>, by a Taylor expansion of this function it can be seen that this term is at most</p>
<table id="S8.E31" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S8.E31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\tau^{2}}{2}\left(\frac{1}{\frac{1}{d}-\tau}+\frac{1}{\frac{1}{d}-\tau}\right)\leq\frac{\tau^{2}}{2}4d." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><msup><mi>τ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>d</mi></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>d</mi></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><msup><mi>τ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\tau^{2}}{2}\left(\frac{1}{\frac{1}{d}-\tau}+\frac{1}{\frac{1}{d}-\tau}\right)\leq\frac{\tau^{2}}{2}4d.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(31)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S8.I1.i2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Summing this up over the <math id="S8.I1.i2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{d}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{d}{2}</annotation></semantics></math> such pairs, we see that the <math id="S8.I1.i2.p1.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="d_{\textsf{KL}}(\theta_{v}\|\pi^{(0)})\leq d^{2}\tau^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">KL</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>τ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\textsf{KL}}(\theta_{v}\|\pi^{(0)})\leq d^{2}\tau^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. To ensure this is at most <math id="S8.I1.i2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta</annotation></semantics></math>, we need <math id="S8.I1.i2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau\leq\sqrt{\Delta/d^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>≤</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau\leq\sqrt{\Delta/d^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S8.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="S8.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To ensure that (<a href="#S8.E27" title="In Lemma VIII.1 (Assouad’s Lemma) ‣ VIII-E Proof of Theorem ‣ VIII Proofs of Theorems ‣ Semantic Smoothing for Language Models via Distribution Estimation and Embeddings" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">27</span></a>) is satisfied in Lemma <a href="#S8.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma VIII.1 (Assouad’s Lemma) ‣ VIII-E Proof of Theorem ‣ VIII Proofs of Theorems ‣ Semantic Smoothing for Language Models via Distribution Estimation and Embeddings" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">VIII.1</span></a>, we need</p>
<table id="S8.EGx13" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_eqnarray ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S8.Ex27"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S8.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\min_{a\in\mathcal{A}}\|\theta_{v}-a\|_{1}+\|a-\theta_{v}^{\prime}\|_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mi>v</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\min_{a\in\mathcal{A}}\|\theta_{v}-a\|_{1}+\|a-\theta_{v}^{\prime}\|_{1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S8.Ex26.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≥</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S8.Ex26.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{\|\theta_{v}-\theta_{v}^{\prime}\|_{1}}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mi>v</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{\|\theta_{v}-\theta_{v}^{\prime}\|_{1}}{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr class="ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S8.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S8.Ex27.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{d_{H}(v,v^{\prime})}{2}(4\tau)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{d_{H}(v,v^{\prime})}{2}(4\tau).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S8.I1.i3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">It can be seen that (<a href="#S8.E27" title="In Lemma VIII.1 (Assouad’s Lemma) ‣ VIII-E Proof of Theorem ‣ VIII Proofs of Theorems ‣ Semantic Smoothing for Language Models via Distribution Estimation and Embeddings" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">27</span></a>) holds for <math id="S8.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda=2\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda=2\tau</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S8.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">4.</span> 
<div id="S8.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Next, we compute</p>
<table id="S8.E32" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S8.E32.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\max_{v,v^{\prime}:d_{H}(v,v^{\prime})=1}d_{\textsf{KL}}(\theta_{v}\|\theta_{v^{\prime}})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">KL</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max_{v,v^{\prime}:d_{H}(v,v^{\prime})=1}d_{\textsf{KL}}(\theta_{v}\|\theta_{v^{\prime}}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(32)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S8.I1.i4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Since the Hamming distance is at most <math id="S8.I1.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S8.I1.i4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S8.I1.i4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> differ only at one coordinate, say <math id="S8.I1.i4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, <math id="S8.I1.i4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{v}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{v}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S8.I1.i4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{v^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{v^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> would be different only at coordinates <math id="S8.I1.i4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2i-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2i-1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S8.I1.i4.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2i</annotation></semantics></math>.
Note that</p>
<table id="S8.EGx14" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_eqnarray ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S8.E33"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S8.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle d_{\textsf{KL}}(\theta_{v}\|\theta_{v^{\prime}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">KL</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle d_{\textsf{KL}}(\theta_{v}\|\theta_{v^{\prime}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S8.Ex28.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S8.Ex28.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left(\frac{1}{d}+\tau v_{i}\right)\log\left(\frac{\frac{1}{d}+\tau v_{i}}{\frac{1}{d}-\tau v_{i}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>d</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>d</mi></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>d</mi></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left(\frac{1}{d}+\tau v_{i}\right)\log\left(\frac{\frac{1}{d}+\tau v_{i}}{\frac{1}{d}-\tau v_{i}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="3" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(33)</span></td></tr>
<tr class="ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S8.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+\left(\frac{1}{d}-\tau v_{i}\right)\log\left(\frac{\frac{1}{d}-\tau v_{i}}{\frac{1}{d}+\tau v_{i}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>d</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>d</mi></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>d</mi></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\left(\frac{1}{d}-\tau v_{i}\right)\log\left(\frac{\frac{1}{d}-\tau v_{i}}{\frac{1}{d}+\tau v_{i}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr class="ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S8.E33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S8.E33.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{(2\tau)^{2}}{\frac{1}{2d}}\leq 8\tau^{2}d." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mfrac></mfrac></mstyle><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>τ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{(2\tau)^{2}}{\frac{1}{2d}}\leq 8\tau^{2}d.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
</ol>
<p id="S8.SS5.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Using Assouad’s Lemma gives a lower bound of</p>
<table id="S8.E34" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S8.E34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\min_{\hat{\pi}}\max_{\pi\in B_{\text{KL}}(\pi^{(0)},\Delta)}\mathbb{E}[\|\pi-\hat{\pi}\|_{1}]\geq\frac{1}{4}\,\frac{d}{2}\,2\tau\,e^{-n8\tau^{2}d}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mtext>KL</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn> 2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>τ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\min_{\hat{\pi}}\max_{\pi\in B_{\text{KL}}(\pi^{(0)},\Delta)}\mathbb{E}[\|\pi-\hat{\pi}\|_{1}]\geq\frac{1}{4}\,\frac{d}{2}\,2\tau\,e^{-n8\tau^{2}d}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(34)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S8.SS5.p3.2" class="ltx_p">To ensure that the term in the exponent is <math id="S8.SS5.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(1)</annotation></semantics></math>, we need for instance <math id="S8.SS5.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n8\tau^{2}d\leq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>τ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n8\tau^{2}d\leq 2</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e. <math id="S8.SS5.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau\leq\frac{1}{\sqrt{4dn}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msqrt></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau\leq\frac{1}{\sqrt{4dn}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Note that to satisfy the first two constraints, <math id="S8.SS5.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau\leq\min\left(\frac{1}{2d},\frac{\sqrt{\Delta}}{d}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><msqrt><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msqrt><mi>d</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau\leq\min\left(\frac{1}{2d},\frac{\sqrt{\Delta}}{d}\right)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S8.SS5.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.SS5.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Pick <math id="S8.SS5.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau=\min\left(\frac{1}{\sqrt{4dn}},\frac{1}{2d},\frac{\sqrt{\Delta}}{d}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msqrt></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><msqrt><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msqrt><mi>d</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau=\min\left(\frac{1}{\sqrt{4dn}},\frac{1}{2d},\frac{\sqrt{\Delta}}{d}\right)</annotation></semantics></math>. This gives a lower bound of</p>
<table id="S8.E35" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S8.E35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{4}\min\left(\sqrt{\frac{d}{4n}},\frac{1}{2},\sqrt{\Delta}\right)e^{-2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac></msqrt><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><msqrt><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msqrt><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{4}\min\left(\sqrt{\frac{d}{4n}},\frac{1}{2},\sqrt{\Delta}\right)e^{-2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(35)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S8.SS5.p4.2" class="ltx_p">This is a lower bound on the expected <math id="S8.SS5.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> norm. To get a lower bound on the KL–divergence itself, we use (<a href="#S8.E26" title="In VIII-E Proof of Theorem ‣ VIII Proofs of Theorems ‣ Semantic Smoothing for Language Models via Distribution Estimation and Embeddings" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">26</span></a>).</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S8.SS6" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S8.SS6.4" class="ltx_text">VIII-F</span> </span><span id="S8.SS6.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Proof of Theorem <a href="#S4.E15" title="In Theorem IV.4 ‣ IV-C Estimated synonymous distribution ‣ IV Distribution Estimation under KL Loss with KL Proximity Side Information ‣ Semantic Smoothing for Language Models via Distribution Estimation and Embeddings" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15</span></a></span></h3>

<div id="S8.SS6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.SS6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">First, note that</p>
<table id="S8.E36" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S8.E36.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{E}[d_{\textsf{KL}}(\pi\|\hat{\pi})]\leq\alpha\mathbb{E}[d_{\textsf{KL}}(\pi\|\hat{\pi}_{\textsf{opt}})]+(1-\alpha)\mathbb{E}[d_{\textsf{KL}}(\pi\|\hat{\pi}^{(0)}_{\textsf{opt}})]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">KL</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>α</mi><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">KL</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">opt</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">KL</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">opt</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[d_{\textsf{KL}}(\pi\|\hat{\pi})]\leq\alpha\mathbb{E}[d_{\textsf{KL}}(\pi\|\hat{\pi}_{\textsf{opt}})]+(1-\alpha)\mathbb{E}[d_{\textsf{KL}}(\pi\|\hat{\pi}^{(0)}_{\textsf{opt}})]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(36)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S8.SS6.p1.2" class="ltx_p">which follows from the convexity of KL divergence.</p>
</div>
<div id="S8.SS6.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.SS6.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Note from Theorem <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem IV.1 ‣ IV Distribution Estimation under KL Loss with KL Proximity Side Information ‣ Semantic Smoothing for Language Models via Distribution Estimation and Embeddings" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">IV.1</span></a> that <math id="S8.SS6.p2.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{E}[d_{\textsf{KL}}(\pi\|\hat{\pi}_{\textsf{opt}})]\leq\frac{d-1}{2n}+o\left(\frac{d}{n}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">KL</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">opt</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mi>o</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[d_{\textsf{KL}}(\pi\|\hat{\pi}_{\textsf{opt}})]\leq\frac{d-1}{2n}+o\left(\frac{d}{n}\right)</annotation></semantics></math>. Note for the other term that</p>
